<title>SWITZERLAND: SWISS-HOLOCAUST-TREATY.</title>
<headline>SWISS-HOLOCAUST-TREATY.</headline>
<dateline>BERNE 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss National Bank (SNB) board member Jean-Pierre Roth said he saw no need to re-open the 1946 Washington Agreement settling the Allies' claims against Switzerland for wartime gold transactions with Nazi Germany.</p>
<p>&quot;There is no new fact to say that renegotiation is necessary,&quot; Roth told reporters in response to a U.S. report that criticised Switzerland's hard line in talks with Allies about returning looted gold it bought from Nazi Germany.</p>
</text>
